		<description>A compact, tough horse directly descended from ancient wild horse breeds. Renowned for its extreme hardiness, thriftiness, and self-sufficiency, it thrives in harsh environments where other breeds would struggle. While smaller in stature and slower than domesticated riding horses, its primitive constitution grants it disease resistance and minimal food requirements.</description>
